Internal os_log codec tests (op-201)

oracle.json contains the eventMessage, formatString and messageType fields of
all 34 op963 and 40 op970 rows from the staged macOS 27 oracle. The source
manifest SHA256 is c14e12c938d7b89dbbf86e01614d5da0a96c9b819d62d863dbfe77570a215d84.
Rmx.Op201 in rmx-implementer regenerates the compiler inputs from those rows.
C fixtures contain Clang builtin call sites and storage getters only. Zig owns
the input selection, bounds-checked capture reader and assertions.

oracle compares every eventMessage byte. The main executable, a linked DSO and
dlopen/RTLD_NODELETE DSO are real native images. For the op963 pointer row it
replays the recorded numeric address, since ASLR addresses differ between runs.
For op970 A03, FreeBSD strerror() returns writable storage and is asserted
private; the byte-exact replay instead uses libc's readonly sys_errlist entry
with identical text. This does not reproduce the native macOS strerror call.
No writable-pointer exemption is added to the codec.

wire asserts the serialized range bytes, scalar formatting, precision, literal
percent and redaction. malformed exercises short inputs, invalid ranges and
formats (including %n), a rejected pointer, and 20,000 random input pairs. The
host sanitizer driver instruments the C codec with Clang ASan and UBSan; its
intentional compiler-input faults verify both instruments are active.

The codec is internal to libc, with hidden symbols and an uninstalled header.
Pointer capture is delegated to a checked reader; rendering has no pointers or
varargs to read. The normal flattened budget is 1024 bytes. The fault profile
uses 1998 bytes to reproduce 1989 string bytes plus header/range/NUL overhead;
that fault budget rests on one macOS 27 call-site measurement, not a general
fault-size contract. Arguments are charged in order, without reserving later
items. No 32-string kernel restriction is applied to user space.

Enablement and record metadata are outside this codec. Disabled/debug and the
crashing Objective-C %@ call in the probes have no stored oracle row to replay.
Object/data/errno/mask descriptors are unsupported; malformed/unsupported inputs
return an error. No public API, installed header, emitter or logd change is made.
